Spec: Feature PictureWidget Thread-Safe Metadata Loading (1.1 / STAB-01)

Purpose:
  Eliminate undefined behavior and race conditions in PictureWidget by decoupling background Exiv2 metadata parsing from Qt GUI widget updates (QTableWidget / QTabWidget), while reading EXIF, IPTC, and XMP metadata in a single Exiv2 file pass.

Platform: C++26 (Linux) / C++23 (Windows, macOS), Qt6

References:
  ../../../desktop-gallery.sdd

Owns:
  ./**

Can modify:
  /include/picture_widget.h
  /src/picture_widget.cpp
  /data/Prioritaetenliste.md

Must:
  Parse EXIF, IPTC, and XMP metadata asynchronously in a worker thread without touching any QWidget, QTableWidget, or QTabWidget instances outside the GUI thread.
  Open and read the image file only once per setImage() call via Exiv2::ImageFactory::open() inside a try/catch block to prevent unhandled Exiv2 exceptions from terminating the worker thread.
  Marshal parsed key/value pairs back to the GUI thread using QMetaObject::invokeMethod(this, ..., Qt::QueuedConnection) so widget updates are safely cancelled if PictureWidget is closed before parsing finishes.
  Ensure include/picture_widget.h has a compliant SPDX & Doxygen MIT header and English documentation comments.

Must not:
  Access or mutate ui->exifTableWidget, ui->iptcTableWidget, ui->xmpTableWidget, or ui->tabWidget from a background thread.
  Block the Qt GUI main thread with synchronous Exiv2 file parsing.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Update include/picture_widget.h with SPDX MIT header, English Doxygen comments, and helper declaration for GUI-thread table population.
  [x] #2 Refactor metadata loading in src/picture_widget.cpp to parse EXIF/IPTC/XMP in a single background pass with exception handling and populate the QTableWidgets on the GUI thread.
  [x] #3 Verify compilation via CMake and mark item 1.1 as completed in data/Prioritaetenliste.md.

Done when:
  cmake --build build succeeds without errors and PictureWidget populates EXIF, IPTC, and XMP tables exclusively on the GUI thread after a single asynchronous Exiv2 read pass.
